.Dd June 18, 2026
.Dt PDCMP 2
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pdcmp
.Nd compare two process descriptors
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libc
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/procdesc.h
.Ft int
.Fn pdcmp "int fd1" "int fd2" "int *result"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn pdcmp
system call compares two process descriptors and reports whether they
refer to the same process.
If both
.Fa fd1
and
.Fa fd2
describe the same process, zero is stored in
.Fa result ;
otherwise a non-zero value is stored.
.Pp
Both arguments must be process descriptor file descriptors.
This is a pure descriptor operation with no ambient authority; it is
usable both inside and outside
.Xr capsicum 4
capability mode.
.Pp
A typical use case is when a supervisor holds process descriptors
obtained from different sources (e.g.,
.Xr pdfork 2
and
.Xr pdself 2
via SCM_RIGHTS) and needs to determine whether two descriptors refer
to the same child.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Rv -std
.Pp
On success, zero is stored in
.Fa result
if both descriptors refer to the same process, or a non-zero value
if they refer to different processes.
.Sh ERRORS
The
.Fn pdcmp
system call fails if:
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EBADF
One of the file descriptor arguments is not a valid open file descriptor.
.It Bq Er EINVAL
One of the file descriptor arguments is not a process descriptor.
.It Bq Er ENOTCAPABLE
One of the file descriptors has insufficient capability rights
.Pq Dv CAP_PDGETPID .
.It Bq Er EFAULT
The
.Fa result
pointer is invalid.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pdgetpid 2 ,
.Xr pdfork 2 ,
.Xr pdself 2 ,
.Xr capsicum 4 ,
.Xr procdesc 4
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn pdcmp
system call first appeared in
.Fx 16.0 .
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Kory Heard
